# Local development only. Copy this file to the ignored root .dev.vars.
# This address belongs to the starter's local mock identity, not to a real owner.
APP_OWNER_EMAIL="seedy@sites.test"
APP_ADMIN_EMAILS=""
TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=""
TELEGRAM_BRIDGE_SECRET=""

# Hosted deployment: configure the verified owner's actual email as a server secret.
# APP_ADMIN_EMAILS is an optional comma/semicolon/newline-separated exact allowlist.
# Never commit production values or grant staff rights from a browser field.
# Telegram remains disabled until the bridge secret is configured on the server.
# Use the same random secret (at least 32 characters) in the separate bot process.
# The Telegram Bot API token belongs only in the bot host's secret environment.
